  "semantics": {
    "argument": "A spot hourly bar stamped `t` closes at `t + 1h`, so the frozen decision instant `T` indexes the bar that has just closed and `close[T]` is knowable at `T`. Every endpoint a feature vector reads is one of `T`, `T-1h`, `T-24h` and `T-168h`, all at or before `T`, on the same official archive the BTC target already uses. Membership is decided bar by bar from what that asset has actually been observed to have by `T`, which the endpoint-only probe below demonstrates rather than asserts.",
